  m_Text: Let's pause here. Do you notice how the ant doesn't have to think about
    the root of the tree anymore? Instead, they only have to think of the parts of
    the path that take place after B7. This type of logic is using something called
    the relative path. It's called the relative path because it starts relative to
    the current location of the ant. The path on the previous page is called the
    absolute path, because it starts at the absolute root of the tree.
